# Line-ending policy: keep the shipped artifacts byte-identical to what they
# were built and tested with.

# Batch files must arrive as CRLF *in the repository*, not merely on checkout.
# core.autocrlf normalises text files to LF when committing, so GitHub would
# hand an LF-only run.bat to anyone downloading the ZIP.  cmd.exe walks a batch
# file line by line looking for CRLF when it resolves "goto" labels, and an
# LF-only launcher is a known way for it to land on the wrong line - failing on
# exactly the machines this file exists to help.  "-text" stores bytes as-is.
*.bat -text

# Explicit for the build output: the executable and its icon are payload, not
# text to be normalised.
*.exe binary
*.ico binary
